# class List extends Array { constructor() { super(); this.tag = 1 } }; list = new List; somethingNoTableLists.takes(list); JSON.stringify(list)
# The list has escaped and the hub of JSON.stringify holds the unknown object in its place. A list finds Array.prototype.toString, which counts as run under every order of flow's rules.
# Under this order it did not count: only a list that the hub saw listed did.
# OPTIONS: testing=DelayFlowRules:1
# RUN: valueflow-solve used
# CHECK: run JSONStringify
# CHECK-NEXT: run ArrayPrototypeToString
# CHECK-NEXT: run ObjectPrototypeToString
# CHECK-NEXT: run ObjectPrototypeValueOf

